                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "43915102",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197987842001",
                            "num_reviews": 164,
                            "playtime_forever": 1278,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 999,
                            "last_played": 1533752458
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I figured this would be a quick and shallow casual pirate game, but it turned out to be much more in depth than I thought.\n\nThis is a tactical pirate/naval warfare strategy game. Most of the time you'll be battling it out at sea or inside cities. The sea, unfortunately, is rather boring with islands spread all around but no land masses to sail around or interact with. The islands feel a little like planets in space. There are no currents or sea monsters (that I've encountered thusfar), so most of the time you'll be sailing from one island to the next, or hunting pirates to battle.\n\nLuckily, that's where the game shines. There are twenty ships spread over four factions. Each faction has their own attack patterns and special moves that you can level up. You can also place captains on ships to give them even more special moves. There is a limit to the amount of crew you can have, so you have to assemble your own ship formations to best suit your strategy. This keeps the battles interesting. Every enemy has a different fleet, and you have to work out a strategy every single fight. Which prevents it from becoming a grind. It gives great satisfaction to beat a stronger opponent with trickery and well thought out plans. The battles rarely last long, so it's also good for quick games.\n\nIf you do tire from fighting, you can follow the story line, do side quests, gather items, go fishing or do some botany. Because why not. You can even fish or pick herbs during battles. Also, there are many special items that give perks or bonuses or one time boosts to further customize your fleet. And you can also purchase paints and patterns similar to Westwind.\n\nSo far I'm finding the game very enjoyable as it is. Add to that a dev who's active in the community and constantly working on improvements and you can't really go wrong with this game.",
